  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for periodic motion (পর্যায়বৃত্ত গতি), book page 37, topic 2.2. The book's four examples: a ceiling fan's blade tip (circular path), Halley's comet round the Sun (elliptical, fast near the Sun and slow far away), a mass bouncing on a spring (straight line) and the heartbeat with an ECG strip. A mark sits on the path; each time the particle comes back to it the count goes up and the repetition is drawn as a bar on a time strip: all bars equal, the period (পর্যায়কাল). The panel works it out as with a stopwatch: পর্যায়কাল = মোট সময় ÷ পুনরাবৃত্তি. The particle carries its velocity arrow; a faint copy stays at the mark and the arrow lands on it again one period later (the same velocity at the same point). The student drags the mark anywhere on the path, switches examples and pauses. Honest time scales (fan slowed 10×, comet 10 years a second and not to scale, spring and heart in real time). Test: 5 tap questions (period from a count, the path's shape, the velocity one period later, a fan slowing down after it is switched off, the heartbeat or which motion is periodic). Phone-first, Bangla.",
  "tags": ["motion", "periodic-motion", "period", "fan", "comet", "spring", "heartbeat", "bangla"],
